838:- Calibration determines scale, zero-point, and possibly clipping ranges from representative data. Static quantization fixes them before inference; dynamic quantization computes activation parameters from current input. `Using activations during calibration ≠ quantizing activations during inference.` Static weight-only deployment can store INT4/INT8 weights while activations stay FP16/BF16; QAT simulates quantization/dequantization during training or fine-tuning, unlike PTQ. QLoRA normally freezes quantized base weights and trains LoRA parameters, so it is not full QAT. [Task 8]
